  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is experimenting in his kitchen. He has NNN spices (numbered 000 through N−1N-1N−1) with types S0,S1,…,SN−1S_0, S_1, \\ldots, S_{N-1}S0​,S1​,…,SN−1​.\n\nYou should answer QQQ queries. Each query is described by two integers LLL and RRR. In each query, Chef wants to use the spices SL,SL+1,…,SRS_L, S_{L+1}, \\ldots, S_RSL​,SL+1​,…,SR​ in some order to make a dish. However, he has no clue about the order in which he should use them to make a perfect dish, so he wants to try all possible orders (sequences created by permuting these R−L+1R-L+1R−L+1 spices) to find out. Tell Chef the number of distinct orders (sequences) of spices he needs to try. Since this number can be very large, compute it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\nTwo sequences of spices are considered different if there is a valid index iii such that the type of the iii-th spice in one sequence is different from the type of the iii-th spice used in the other sequence.\n\nNote that the input is encoded so that you have to answer the queries online.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,Q≤3⋅1051 \\le N, Q \\le 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Si≤1091 \\le S_i \\le 10^91≤Si​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "0≤L1,L2,R1,R2≤N−10 \\le L_1, L_2, R_1, R_2 \\le N-10≤L1​,L2​,R1​,R2​≤N−1",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** 1≤N,Q≤1031 \\le N, Q \\le 10^31≤N,Q≤103",
      "**Subtask #2 (40 points):**",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\le N, Q \\le 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "L1=R1=0L_1 = R_1 = 0L1​=R1​=0",
      "**Subtask #3 (30 points):** 1≤N,Q≤1051 \\le N, Q \\le 10^51≤N,Q≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers S0,S1,S2,…,SN−1S_0, S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{N-1}S0​,S1​,S2​,…,SN−1​.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains four space-separated integers L1L_1L1​, L2L_2L2​, R1R_1R1​ and R2R_2R2​ describing a query. The parameters LLL and RRR can be calculated in the following way:\n\nLet's denote the answer to the previous query by aaa; for the first query, a=0a = 0a=0.\nCalculate L=(L1⋅a+L2)%NL = (L_1 \\cdot a + L_2) \\% NL=(L1​⋅a+L2​)%N and R=(R1⋅a+R2)%NR = (R_1 \\cdot a + R_2) \\% NR=(R1​⋅a+R2​)%N.\nThen, if L&gt;RL \\gt RL&gt;R, swap LLL and RRR.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer — the number of distinct orders of spices modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.",
